---
/* eslint-disable better-tailwindcss/no-unknown-classes */
import fireUrl from "./fire.webp?url";
import pyre1 from "./pyre-1.webp?url";
import pyre2 from "./pyre-2.webp?url";
import pyre3 from "./pyre-3.webp?url";
import pyre4 from "./pyre-4.webp?url";

const pyreLevels = [
  { src: pyre1, top: 94.5, h: 48 },
  { src: pyre2, top: 81.5, h: 48 },
  { src: pyre3, top: 52.9, h: 62 },
  { src: pyre4, top: 27.2, h: 65 },
];
---

<article class="wd-page wd-verso wd-hunter">
  <span class="wd-pageno">4 · hunter</span>
  <h2 class="wd-full wd-hunter-title">
    Hunter
    <span class="wd-hunter-booktitle">Why Would You Fight a Dragon?</span>
  </h2>
  <section class="wd-pyre wd-span-2" style="grid-row: span 4">
    <h3 class="wd-rubric">Pyre</h3>
    <div
      class="wd-pyre-visual"
      role="img"
      aria-label="Pyre track, four levels from base to tip"
    >
      <img class="wd-pyre-img" src={fireUrl} alt="" />
      {
        pyreLevels.map(({ src, top, h }) => (
          <>
            <div class="wd-pyre-tick" style={`top: ${top}%`} />
            <img
              class="wd-pyre-num"
              src={src}
              alt=""
              style={`top: ${top}%; block-size: ${((h / 1332) * 100).toFixed(2)}%`}
            />
          </>
        ))
      }
    </div>
    <p class="wd-hint">
      Mark circles or slide a paperclip. <br />Fill four and you're <strong
        >consumed</strong
      >.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="wd-span-4 wd-fields">
    <div class="wd-field">
      <span class="wd-field-name">Name</span>
      <span class="wd-line"></span>
      <span class="wd-examples wd-stat-desc italic">
        e.g. Sigurd, Vanda, Skuba, Bastian, Fleur, Martha, Wulf, Maud, Juro, Orm
      </span>
    </div>
    <div class="wd-field">
      <span class="wd-field-name">Class</span>
      <span class="wd-line"></span>
      <label class="wd-bellow">
        <input type="checkbox" data-checkbox-marker="x" />
        <span>Bellow</span>
      </label>
      <span class="wd-examples wd-stat-desc italic">
        e.g. Knight, King, Bowman, Wizard, Maiden, Mutant, Trickster, Saint
      </span>
    </div>
    <div class="wd-field">
      <span class="wd-field-name">Look</span>
      <span class="wd-line"></span>
      <span class="wd-examples wd-stat-desc italic">
        e.g. radiant, fair, pale, gaunt, scarred, sooty, grim, old, white hair,
        wild eyes
      </span>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="wd-span-4">
    <h3 class="wd-rubric">Stats</h3>
    <div class="h-[1.5mm]"></div>
    {
      [
        ["Body", "physical strength and stamina"],
        ["Wits", "mental acuity and perception"],
        ["Soul", "arcane potency and spiritual force"],
      ].map(([stat, meaning]) => (
        <div class="wd-stat-row">
          <span class="wd-stat-name">{stat}</span>
          <span class="wd-stat-desc italic">({meaning})</span>
          <span class="wd-stat-slot" />
        </div>
      ))
    }
    <p class="wd-hint">
      Distribute −2 to +2 so the total equals +1, or choose one from <span
        class="font-hand tracking-tighter"
        >(+2,0,−1), (+1,+1,−1), (+1,0,0), (+2,+1,−2)</span
      > and swap. When it drops to −3, <strong class="font-semibold"
        >Turn to Ash</strong
      >.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="wd-span-2">
    <h3 class="wd-rubric">Goal</h3>
    <ul class="wd-goal-list">
      {
        [
          "Glory",
          "Greed",
          "Knowledge",
          "Love",
          "Oath",
          "Power",
          "Vengeance",
        ].map((goal) => (
          <li>
            <input type="checkbox" data-checkbox-marker="x" />
            <span>{goal}</span>
          </li>
        ))
      }
      <li>
        <input type="checkbox" data-checkbox-marker="x" />
        <span class="wd-line"></span>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>
  <section class="wd-span-2 wd-notes">
    <span class="wd-rose" aria-hidden="true">❦</span>
    <h3 class="wd-rubric">Notes</h3>
  </section>
  <section class="wd-span-4">
    <div class="wd-xp-head">
      <h3 class="wd-rubric">XP</h3>
      {
        [1, 2, 3, 4].map(() => (
          <input type="checkbox" data-checkbox-marker="x" />
        ))
      }
    </div>
    <p class="wd-hint">
      Mark 1 XP when you roll a 6−, or your Goal leads you into danger. <br />
      4 XP and a moment of rest: raise a stat by +1 (up to +3) or clear 1 Pyre.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="wd-span-3 wd-howto">
    <h3 class="wd-rubric">How to Play</h3>
    <p>
      If you do it, do it in the fiction. Describe how and what it looks like.
    </p>
    <p>
      If it triggers a move, the DM will call it. If it fits no move, don't
      roll: it happens.
    </p>
    <p>
      When everything's on fire and the Dragon's about to eat you, action calls
      for <strong>Face Fury</strong>.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="wd-span-3 wd-principles">
    <h3 class="wd-rubric">Player Principles</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Begin and end with the fiction.</li>
      <li>Bind your story to other Hunters.</li>
      <li>Be bold, take risks, embrace the fire.</li>
      <li>Pay attention, ask questions, offer suggestions.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</article>
